"""Approximate a sparse mixture of spelling and phrase responses.

A `na` fragment is strongest after n/d/t/s; lowercase `anna` is another
positive cue. Three Dutch function-word occurrences in the document enable
larger go/after-form responses. Chinese means, strengthening, and change
constructions are positive; a single Han character after 不 is weakly
negative, except the intensifying 不胜. Other tokens are normally zero.
The small spelling rules also cover N+A and e+ith/e+ige boundaries.
These are partial lexical heuristics, not a general semantic analysis.
