Key-ending colons are positive; quotes starting the next key are negative.
First keys named 'name' are stronger, while 'type'/'line' headers are weaker.
Brackets distinguish objects from arrays and function arguments. Escaped code,
source line numbers and diff prefixes are handled as formatting. Everything
else is zero except small quote/comma/brace punctuation responses, leaving
background lexical variation unexplained. Two secondary responses mark a
single blank after a literal newline escape and the digit completing a
lowercase escaped UTF-8 E2 byte.
