"""An onset pulse: large on the first token, nearly zero after it.

Its size depends mainly on whether the opening token is a space-prefixed
word. Case, script, punctuation, indentation and grammatical classes refine the
amplitude. Repeating the opening token keeps the pulse alive; the first
different token turns it off. Document boundaries restart this rule.
