"""A sparse lexical approximation: occurrence, life, and publication.

Strong positive rules recognize 'happen/occur' words and word fragments in
Chinese, Japanese, Korean, Vietnamese, and Thai. Life/origination words and
Japanese 発 have weaker responses; distribution and development supply a few
negative contrasts. English publication metadata is case-sensitive: 'Posted
on' is positive, 'Published by' negative. These are specific lexical rules,
not a general semantic classifier. Middle dots and fragment starts have
separate offsets. The remaining positions return zero.
